663	+// overlay over its base layer at the same position. Nothing may be drawn
664	+// closer to the camera than its geometry really is, and nothing may be pushed
665	+// behind the nodes around it: either one hides whatever is drawn right on top
666	+// of a node (the selection outline, things lying on the node such as a track),
667	+// and the overlay must never end up behind its own base layer.
668	+//
