    "explanation": "Both added test files are organized into clearly commented sections (e.g. '---- framed glass ----', '---- turned node boxes ----', '---- node box sides ----', '---- rails ----', '---- fences ----', '---- wall-mounted outlines ----'), each with a short explanatory comment, descriptive TEST_CASE names that double as behavior specifications, and small focused helper functions (render, covered, hasFace, sameBoxes) that make the geometric assertions legible."
  },
  "anti_cheating_measures": {
    "outcome": "pass",
    "explanation": "The injected bug patches are applied, then deleted in the same Dockerfile RUN layer before the harbor_base commit/tag is created, so no diff or history reveals the defects. Only assets/recording.mp4 is copied into the image (explicitly not the whole assets/ folder, since ASSET_MANIFEST.json spells out the bugs in words). tests/ and solution/ are never copied into the image (test.patch and fix.patch only exist in the task repo, applied at grading time via test.sh). The agent runs with network_mode = 'no-network', preventing it from fetching the real upstream fix commit from GitHub. test.sh resets any path test.patch touches from the immutable harbor_base tag before applying hidden tests, preventing tampering with the harness."
  },
  "structured_data_schema": {
    "outcome": "not_applicable",
    "explanation": "This is a C++ source-code bug-fix task graded by compiling and running Catch2 unit tests against the existing engine source; it does not require the agent to produce or conform to any structured output schema (JSON/CSV/API/DB)."
  },
  "pinned_dependencies": {
    "outcome": "pass",
